      "role": "user",
      "content": "I'm looking at the sheet now. Even with the weighted average, hide the 85% in Diamond for a second—look at the kill-to-death ratio and the gold lead at 10 mins. It's statistically absurd. If we ship him like this, the pro scene is going to be a nightmare and players are going to complain about the game being broken. \n\nAre you sure we shouldn't just tone down his ability cooldowns now? I'd rather deal with a small nerf today than a massive community backlash and a balance crisis a week after launch.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I completely agree with you, the kill-to-death ratio and gold lead at 10 minutes are indeed concerning. However, I've been reviewing the data from our internal testing, and I think we've identified a few key factors that contribute to Xylos's dominance. It's not just about his ability cooldowns, but also the synergy between his abilities and the current meta. If we nerf his cooldowns too much, it could disrupt the balance of the game and create new problems.\n\nThat being said, I do think we need to make some adjustments to Xylos's kit. I've been in talks with our design team, and we're considering a few tweaks to his abilities. I think a more targeted nerf to his ultimate ability could help bring him more in line with the rest of the meta. But I'm not convinced that a cooldown nerf is the way to go. We need to be careful not to create a new imbalance.",
